  "nhl": {
    "sport": "nhl",
    "name": "Blowout Bounce-Back",
    "rule": "Bet the moneyline on a SMALL favorite (about -101 to -150) whose previous game was a puck-line disaster: lost as the puck-line favorite, or lost by 4+ goals as an underdog.",
    "why": "NHL results are very noisy (goaltending, shooting luck), but the market overreacts to the most recent ugly result. Good teams coming off a bad loss are priced too cheaply. NFL has the same overreaction pattern (see the NFL runner-up).",
